  "label": "LSTM (FlowCast's network, retrained on the bake-off bank)",
  "family": "ssm",
  "family_label": "State-space and recurrent models (LSTM)",
  "released": "r1",
  "assumption": "A small learned state is carried from day to day and updated through gates: each day the network decides how much of each memory cell to keep (forget gate), what to add (input gate) and what to release into the output. That is a learned version of a bucket model: snow, soil and groundwater stores that fill and drain. It is FlowCast v1.0's choice and the in-bake-off control: same network, same loss, same bank as the three other sequence arms.",
  "core": "One LSTM layer with 64 units over the 29 daily channels, dropout 0.1 before the head: exactly FlowCast v1.0's network (`models/flowcast/training/src/model.py`), retrained from scratch on the harness bank with FlowCast's recipe.",
  "rungs": [
   {
    "id": "r0",
    "change": "FlowCast r1b recipe exactly (3000 steps x 32 windows)",
    "decision": "base",
    "why": "the control: FlowCast's network and recipe on the shared bank. Scores below FlowCast v1.0 as released (sim 0.426, dev 0.425) at the same recipe; 3 seeds agree on sim (0.409-0.410), so the gap is not seed noise (see notes)."
   },
   {
    "id": "r1",
    "change": "2x training: 6000 steps (cosine over 6000)",
    "decision": "released",
    "why": "sim +0.016 over r0 (> 0.01 margin; seed noise on sim is ~0.001) and dev 0.441 >= 0.95 x 0.391: kept. Released (r2 did not beat it)."
   },
   {
    "id": "r2",
    "change": "4x training: 12000 steps",
    "decision": "rejected",
    "why": "sim +0.003 over r1 (< 0.01 margin; paired bootstrap -0.011..+0.017), dev 0.440 vs 0.441: no gain from more training beyond 6000 steps."
   }
  ],
  "noise_checks": [
   "seed1",
   "seed2"
  ],
  "limits": [
   "Ungauged only: it never reads streamflow, so it cannot correct a basin's own water balance (ERA5-Land undercatch, losses). The water-yield multiplier p1 is learned only as a prior from attributes.",
   "Memory is limited to the 365-day warm-up of each block (FlowCast's design): multi-year groundwater carry-over is not represented.",
   "Dev seed noise is large: three seeds of r0 gave dev 0.391, 0.431, 0.404 on the same sim score (0.409-0.410). Dev differences under ~0.04 between arms are not meaningful.",
   "Bands are raw pinball quantiles; FlowCast widened its 90 % band x1.08 on dev, this arm does not (arm C's conformal layer calibrates every arm)."
  ],
  "notes": [
   "Retraining FlowCast's exact recipe (3000 steps) on the harness bank gave sim 0.410 (3 seeds: 0.410, 0.410, 0.409) against 0.426 for the released FlowCast v1.0 weights on the same frozen set. Candidate causes, not resolved: the harness train bank was built with the repo's latest WaterSim (6 files differ from the copy FlowCast used; the val set reproduces FlowCast's), and torch initialisation/dropout streams. At 6000 steps the retrained network matches FlowCast v1.0 on sim (0.4255 vs 0.426) and is higher on dev (0.441 vs 0.425; within dev seed noise).",
   "The quick validation printed during training (first 200 val runs) is monitoring only; every decision uses harness evaluate.py on all 800 runs + the dev gate."
  ]
 },
 "tcn": {
  "arm_id": "seq_tcn",
  "label": "TCN (dilated causal 1-D CNN)",
  "family": "cnn1d",
  "family_label": "1-D convolutional network (temporal convolutional network)",
  "released": "r1",
  "assumption": "The flow today is a learned function of the weather at fixed lags. A stack of causal convolutions reads the last 1, 2, 4 ... 256 days at fixed offsets (receptive field 1,023 days, more than the 730-day window), the same way on every date, and builds longer features with depth. There is no explicit store carried forward: memory is a fixed-lag pattern detector, like a bank of learned unit hydrographs with nonlinear mixing between layers.",
  "core": "Linear 29 -> 26 channels, then 9 residual blocks (pre-LayerNorm, causal convolution with kernel 3 and dilation 1, 2, 4, ..., 256 days, GELU, 1x1 channel mix), final LayerNorm, dropout 0.1 before the head.",
  "rungs": [
   {
    "id": "r0",
    "change": "base: FlowCast's training recipe (3000 steps)",
    "decision": "base",
    "why": "first rung; same recipe as the LSTM control's r0."
   },
   {
    "id": "r1",
    "change": "2x training: 6000 steps (cosine over 6000)",
    "decision": "released",
    "why": "sim +0.015 over r0 (paired bootstrap +0.001..+0.032) and dev 0.420 >= 0.95 x 0.412: kept. Released (r2 did not beat it)."
   },
   {
    "id": "r2",
    "change": "gated activations (WaveNet tanh x sigmoid) instead of GELU; channels 26 -> 20 to keep 26.9k parameters; 6000 steps",
    "decision": "rejected",
    "why": "sim 0.405 vs 0.416 (-0.012) although dev 0.425: multiplicative gating did not help the convolution."
   }
  ],
  "limits": [
   "Ungauged only: it never reads streamflow.",
   "Memory is a fixed set of lags inside the 730-day window (each 365-day block gets its own 365-day warm-up): no multi-year carry-over, and the response to a storm is shaped by learned kernels rather than by a store that depends on how wet the basin already is (that dependence can only come from the nonlinear mixing between layers).",
   "Dev seed noise (measured on the LSTM control) is ~0.02 sd: dev differences under ~0.04 between arms are not meaningful.",
   "Bands are raw pinball quantiles (no dev widening). Its 90 % band is the widest of the four sequence arms on sim val (coverage 0.97)."
